    PnP staff: one race-tolerant roster pagination per baseline, fail-closed reuse
    
    baseline() paginated the >2600-agent Antonina registry once per live gap,
    exceeding 120s and spuriously raising 'inconsistent agent roster' when an
    insertion shifted the offset window. roster() now fetches bounded concurrent
    waves, dedupes cross-page repeats (insertions), but fails closed on an in-page
    duplicate, unreadable page, malformed id or unbounded cursor. baseline() fetches
    one snapshot reused by every dispatch(); direct dispatch() still fetches its own.
    Add a fail-closed guard against two live workers on one bound workspace. Dispatch
    semantics (exact-cwd adoption, reusable states, uncertainty refusal, focus
    re-check under staff.lock) are unchanged.
    
    Tests: idempotence, exact workspace reuse, duplicate/uncertain refusal and the
    pagination race; python3 tests/pnp-allocator.py 24/24 OK.

